   if (Old_arrListContainsX)
   {
       Assert.LessThanOrEqual(New_arrListIndexOfX, Old_arrListIndexOfX + 1);
   }
   ```

5. `// @@@ new array contains no more instances of old x, and no new instances of x`
   This comment suggests that we need to assert that after modifying the array by adding, removing, or setting element x, the new array no longer contains any old instances of x and no new instances of x. We can achieve this by checking that the old x is no longer present in the new array (`arrList.Contains(Old_x) == false`) and that no new instances of x are present in the new array (`arrList.Contains(New_Ret) == false`).
   Here's the corresponding Assert statements:
   ```cs
